# Security and Best Practices

## API Key Management

### Environment Variables
- Store all sensitive data in `.env` file
- Never commit API keys to version control
- Use different keys for testing and production
- Rotate keys regularly

### Key Validation
```go
// Validate API keys on startup
if cfg.APIKey == "" || cfg.APISecret == "" {
    logger.ErrorFmt("API keys not configured. Set BINANCE_API_KEY and BINANCE_SECRET_KEY in .env")
    return
}
```

### Key Masking in Logs
```go
// Always mask sensitive data in logs
log.Info().
    Str("API_KEY", "***").
    Str("API_SECRET", "***").
    Msg("Bot started with config")
```

## Simulation Mode Safety

### Default to Simulation
- Always default to simulation mode
- Require explicit configuration for live trading
- Implement multiple confirmation steps
- Use clear visual indicators

```go
if cfg.SimulationMode {
    logger.InfoFmt("MODE: %s %s", logger.Green("SIMULATION"), logger.Italic("(no real trades)"))
} else {
    logger.InfoFmt("MODE: %s %s", logger.Yellow("LIVE TRADING"), logger.Italic("(real trades will be placed)"))
}
```

### Configuration Validation
- Validate all configuration values
- Check for reasonable limits
- Prevent dangerous configurations
- Require explicit confirmation for live trading

## Financial Safety

### Amount Limits
- Implement maximum trade amounts
- Validate against account balance
- Use conservative default amounts
- Implement daily/hourly limits

### Risk Management
- Set maximum loss limits
- Implement stop-loss mechanisms
- Monitor account balance continuously
- Alert on unusual activity

### Fee Validation
- Validate fee rates are reasonable
- Check for minimum profit thresholds
- Account for all trading costs
- Monitor slippage and spreads

## Code Security

### Input Validation
- Validate all external inputs
- Sanitize user-provided data
- Check for reasonable ranges
- Prevent injection attacks

### Error Information
- Don't expose sensitive information in errors
- Log errors securely
- Use generic error messages for users
- Keep detailed logs internal

### Dependency Management
- Keep dependencies up to date
- Use only trusted packages
- Audit dependencies regularly
- Pin specific versions

## Network Security

### HTTPS/TLS
- Use secure connections for all API calls
- Validate SSL certificates
- Implement proper timeout handling
- Use connection pooling

### Rate Limiting
- Respect API rate limits
- Implement exponential backoff
- Monitor API usage
- Handle rate limit errors gracefully

## Operational Security

### Logging Security
- Don't log sensitive data
- Use structured logging
- Implement log rotation
- Secure log file permissions

### Process Security
- Run with minimal privileges
- Use dedicated user accounts
- Implement process monitoring
- Secure file permissions

### Backup and Recovery
- Regular configuration backups
- Test recovery procedures
- Document emergency procedures
- Maintain audit trails

